during the 2008 presidential campaign  michelle obama was asked on the tonight  show about the cost of her wardrobe  [Music]  actually this is a j crew ensemble  really wow  j.crew clothing would become a staple in  the former first lady's wardrobe  elevating the brand's image from preppy  basics to professional  yet affordable chic but recently the  apparel brand has struggled with  slumping sales and a debt load that  ultimately led the retailer to seek  bankruptcy protection  in court filings the company cited  losses incurred because of coronavirus  lockdowns but analysts say the brand  also lost touch with consumers with  styles that appeared more suited for the  runway  than for everyday life here's how j.crew  filed for bankruptcy  j.crew formerly known as popular  merchandise inc  emerged in 1983 as a catalog only  retailer  it offered a pioneering line of casual  fashion built on affordable weathered  chinos and simple crewneck t-shirts  well they were really the preppy chic  brand  sort of preppy with a twist the kind of  clothes that you know you could wear to  the office but also the perfect  weekend clothes the brand opened its  first retail store in 1989  and over the next decade found its home  in malls across the country  many of the brand styles can be  attributed to jenna lyons  who was first hired as a designer in  1990.  her design influence grew the brand by  attracting both luxury  and middle-class customers former gap  ceo mickey drexler joined the company in  2003  and promoted lines to creative director  a few years later  mickey drexler was best known for  turning gap into a cultural icon in the  1990s  he came to j crew and sort of had a  second act  and jenna lyons was sort of his creative  right hand  woman so to speak she turned things like  sequins where  you would think would you only wear sort  of out on a saturday night you know all  of a sudden you could  you know wear them during the day and  she kind of really glammed up the brand  in 2006 drexler founded the successful  companion brand madewell  j crew also went public that same year  only to be taken private again five  years later  in a leveraged buyout that saddled the  company with debt  not too long after sales began to flag  starting in 2014 j  crew experienced six straight years of  losses and the company  started looking for ways to cut back and  attract new customers  well they started to get a bit too glam  and that this is where some of the  critics started blaming jenna that  her style became to brooklyn for their  kind of j cruz mainstream  customers and then on top of that they  ended up with quality  and fit problems you know the quality  became inconsistent  customers kind of just lost faith in the  brand  in 2017 with the company still  floundering lions departed and drexler  stepped down as ceo  and the brand narrowly avoided  bankruptcy as part of a controversial  debt swap  that moved its intellectual property  beyond the reach of creditors  they were just caught a little bit  flat-footed and didn't act fast enough  to  you know um develop e-commerce to  develop  you know all the things now that we sort  of expect from a retailer  heading into 2020 j.crew planned to  raise cash by spinning off its madewell  chain through an ipo but plans came to a  halt as coronavirus lockdowns forced the  retailer to close some 500 stores  in court filings the brand said it  expected to lose 900 million dollars in  sales because of lockdowns  putting it in a position where it  couldn't pay its debts  on may 4th 2020 j.crew filed for  bankruptcy  you know j crew has a smaller footprint  than a lot of other retailers  and they didn't overexpand so that's  positive for them  they are in a position where they're not  going to probably have to close  hundreds of stores they also have a new  ceo  and you know her mission was sort of to  restore the brand to its former glory  you know getting back to the quality and  the fit that  customers loved and kind of the classic  styles  as the retailer looks to navigate its  way out of bankruptcy  it will also try to recapture customers  who once looked for clothes that could  be worn on any occasion  even inauguration day
 

